From 65dd5d8977245b5c6606feb9efbc79a54acd5bcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Port <port@local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:13:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] misc: add WL2866D camera power management IC driver

Add a clean Kernel 6.12 port of the downstream Xiaomi WL2866D driver
used by the Topaz/Tapas camera power path. Preserve the vendor device
tree properties, default register table, identity check, board init
sequence, four camera supply outputs, exported
wl2866d_camera_power_control() helper and /dev/wl2866d register format.

Modernize the implementation with an allocated reference-counted
device, device property parsing with range validation, GPIO descriptor
handling, bounded I2C transfers, a dynamic root-only misc minor and
per-file register offsets. Correct the downstream misc semantics so
read count is a byte capacity, read returns copied bytes, writes only
process complete validated records and llseek returns the selected
register.

The outputs are disabled at the end of probe, as downstream does. This
is not a regulator provider and does not add any camera sensor, CAMSS
or Spectra support.

Signed-off-by: Port <port@local>
